    "q-78497": {
      "dom_id": "step-q78497",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "If $F=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]$, then ${F}^{2}=$",
      "worked_solution": "To find ${F}^{2},$ we multiply $F$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{2} & =F\\cdot F \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 12 \\\\ 4 & 19\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
