      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "If $B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$, then ${B}^{2}=$",
      "worked_solution": "To find ${B}^{2},$ we multiply $B$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{2} & =B\\cdot B \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 7 & 2 \\\\ -5 & -8 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
