    "q-130673": {
      "dom_id": "step-q130673",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}].$  Find $f(A)$ if $f(X)={X}^{2}+X-1.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}+X-1 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}+X-I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(A)={A}^{2}+A-I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${A}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(A):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & ={A}^{2}+A-I \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+3-1 & 0-2+0 \\\\ 0+4+0 & 1-3-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
